msgid "Response Format"
msgstr "Response Format"

#: providers/models/core/models/model.py:269
msgid ""
"Set a response format, ensure the output from llm is a valid code block "
"as possible, such as JSON, XML, etc."
msgstr ""
"Set a response format, ensure the output from llm is a valid code block "
"as possible, such as JSON, XML, etc."

#: providers/models/core/models/model.py:275
msgid "JSON Schema"
msgstr "JSON Schema"

#: providers/models/core/models/model.py:276
msgid ""
"Define a JSON schema to structure and validate the LLM's response. The "
"schema should follow JSON Schema specification format."
msgstr ""
"Define a JSON schema to structure and validate the LLM's response. The "
"schema should follow JSON Schema specification format."

#: providers/models/deepseek/deepseek_schema.py:5
msgid "DeepSeek"
msgstr "DeepSeek"

#: providers/models/deepseek/deepseek_schema.py:6
msgid "Models provided by deepseek, such as deepseek-chat、deepseek-coder."
msgstr "Models provided by deepseek, such as deepseek-chat、deepseek-coder."

#: providers/models/deepseek/deepseek_schema.py:12
msgid "Get your API Key from deepseek"
msgstr "Get your API Key from deepseek"

#: providers/models/deepseek/deepseek_schema.py:33
msgid "Custom API endpoint URL"
msgstr "Custom API endpoint URL"

#: providers/models/deepseek/deepseek_schema.py:34
msgid "Base URL, e.g. https://api.deepseek.com/v1 or https://api.deepseek.com"
msgstr "Base URL, e.g. https://api.deepseek.com/v1 or https://api.deepseek.com"

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:22
msgid ""
"Control the diversity and randomness of generated results. The smaller "
"the value, the more rigorous it is; the larger the value, the more "
"divergent it is."
msgstr ""
"Control the diversity and randomness of generated results. The smaller "
"the value, the more rigorous it is; the larger the value, the more "
"divergent it is."

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:45
msgid ""
"Control the randomness of generated results. The smaller the value, the "
"weaker the randomness; the larger the value, the stronger the randomness."
" Generally speaking, you can adjust one of the two parameters top_p and "
"temperature."
msgstr ""
"Control the randomness of generated results. The smaller the value, the "
"weaker the randomness; the larger the value, the stronger the randomness."
" Generally speaking, you can adjust one of the two parameters top_p and "
"temperature."

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:54
msgid "Log Probabilities"
msgstr "Log Probabilities"

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:56
msgid ""
"Whether to return the log probability of the output token. If true, "
"returns the log probability of each output token in the content of "
"message."
msgstr ""
"Whether to return the log probability of the output token. If true, "
"returns the log probability of each output token in the content of "
"message."

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:63
msgid "Top Log Probabilities"
msgstr "Top Log Probabilities"

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:68
msgid ""
"An integer N between 0 and 20, specifying that each output position "
"returns the top N tokenswith output probability, and returns the "
"logarithmic probability of these tokens. When specifying this parameter, "
"logprobs must be true."
msgstr ""
"An integer N between 0 and 20, specifying that each output position "
"returns the top N tokens with output probability, and returns the "
"logarithmic probability of these tokens. When specifying this parameter, "
"logprobs must be true."

#: providers/models/deepseek/llm/schemas/deepseek_chat.py:80
msgid ""
"A number between -2.0 and 2.0. If the value is positive, new tokens are "
"penalized basedon their frequency of occurrence in existing text,reducing"
" the likelihood that the model will repeat the same content."
msgstr ""
"A number between -2.0 and 2.0. If the value is positive, new tokens are "
"penalized based on their frequency of occurrence in existing text, "
"reducing the likelihood that the model will repeat the same content."

